racle (0.87).\n- 2-LF deployable config: 0.978 in-domain but collapses to 2.81% coverage on OpenHands cross-agent.\n\n**Key tables/results:**\n- Table 1: Matched-scope GB=0.952 vs Probe=0.618 (+33.4pp), 95% CI [29.8, 37.2], p<0.001\n- Table 2: LLM judges on OH: Claude few-shot-CoT 0.762, GPT-5.5 0.698, Structural GB 0.967\n- Table 3: Cross-agent consistency: Structural GB drops only 2.8pp (SWE→OH), Claude FS-CoT drops 3.7pp\n- Table 4: Gold set (491 windows, 3 annotators): GB 0.839 vs MV 0.798 (+4.2pp, p<0.001). SWE subset: GB 0.792 vs MV 0.765 (p=0.034). Inter-annotator κ=0.42 on SWE.\n- Table 5: 2-LF cross-agent: coverage collapses from 30.3% (3-LF) to 2.81% (2-LF conf≥2)\n- Table 6: Stagnation tail decomposition: 13.7% tail, 43.5% recovery, 7.8% true waste\n- Table 7: Early termination: k=3 saves 7.6% compute, 18.5% false termination\n- Table 8: Pareto AUC: Oracle 0.87, Structural 0.56, Random 0.43\n- Table 9-12: Appendix per-agent breakdowns and bootstrap CIs\n\n**Experiment design context (from review_context.yaml):**\nThe review context reveals the paper is aware of these weaknesses:\n- Stagnation is intermittent, not terminal — recovery bursts undermine the \"compute waste\" narrative\n- Early termination faces a fundamental precision-recall dilemma with no good operating point\n- 2-LF deployable config is non-deployable cross-agent (cmd_rep fires only 5.39% on OH)\n- The paper pivoted to a \"3-claim detection paper\" after intervention results (Claim 4) failed\n- Gold set on SWE shows 20pp drop from in-domain (0.995→0.792), exposing LF label dependence\n\n**Your task:** Provide a detailed review covering:\n1. **Summary** (2-3 sentences)\n2. **Strengths** (bulleted, with specifics)\n3. **Weaknesses** (bulleted, with specifics — focus on methodology, experimental design, statistical rigor, circularity concerns, evaluation fairness)\n4. **Questions for authors**\n5. **Missing experiments or analyses**\n6. **Minor issues**\n7. **Overall assessment** (score with justification)\n8. **Confidence** (1-5)\n\nBe rigorous. Consider: circularity of evaluation, gold set size and annotator agreement, whether the \"zero-shot dominance\" claim survives scrutiny, whether negative results are well-characterized enough to be contributions, statistical rigor of comparisons, and practical significance."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01CeSkggptN9gSpARBPABS1z","session_id":"62a285b4-2e65-40ae-891e-0aaa22cfb53a","uuid":"4f17ad13-1f07-47b4-9295-1bd164b79b85","timestamp":"2026-05-15T15:44:27.196Z"}
